```

## Database

### Prisma Usage

- Use Prisma for database operations
- Define types based on Prisma schema
- Use Prisma Client for database queries
- Keep schema in `prisma/schema.prisma`

### Database Example

```typescript
import { PrismaClient } from '@prisma/client';

const prisma = new PrismaClient();

interface User {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  email: string;
}

const getUser = async (id: number): Promise<User | null> => {
  return await prisma.user.findUnique({
    where: { id },
  });
};
```

## TypeScript

### Type Definitions

- Define interfaces for all props
- Use strict typing
- Avoid `any` type completely
- Use `unknown` for unknown types

### Type Example

```typescript
interface UserProps {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  email: string;
  avatar?: string;
}

interface ApiResponse<T> {
  data: T;
  status: number;
  message: string;
}
```
